@page "/configuration"

<PageTitle>Font Awesome Blazor Configuration</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid mt-3 mb-4">
    <h1>Configuration</h1>

    <p>
        Every value the library can default &mdash; icon style, typeface, size, and accessibility mode &mdash; can be
        set in two places. Both are pure host-side configuration: no JavaScript interop, no runtime discovery.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Application-wide defaults (dependency injection)</h2>

    <p>
        Register <code>FontAwesomeOptions</code> once at startup. Any component that does not set the value
        itself picks it up:
    </p>

    <CodeSnippet Language="csharp">
        <Snippet>
            builder.Services.AddJeninFontAwesome(options =&gt; {
                options.IconStyle = IconStyle.Solid;
                options.IconSize = IconSize.X03;
                options.Typeface = Typeface.Classic;
            });
        </Snippet>
    </CodeSnippet>

    <p class="mb-4">
        The icon picker has its own optional registration. It is not required &mdash; without it the picker falls back
        to <code>IconMetadataProvider.Default</code> &mdash; but registering keeps a single shared provider when several
        pickers live in the same app:
    </p>

    <CodeSnippet Language="csharp">
        <Snippet>
            builder.Services.AddJeninFontAwesomeIconPicker();
        </Snippet>
    </CodeSnippet>

    <h2 class="mt-4">2. Subtree defaults (cascading component)</h2>

    <p>
        Wrap a region in <code>FontAwesomeDefaults</code> to scope defaults without touching DI. Nested usages merge
        with &mdash; and override &mdash; their ancestors, and an explicit parameter on any descendant still wins:
    </p>

    <div class="configuration-page sample-page">
        <SampleTabs>
            <Tabs>
                <SampleTab Text="Blazor">
                    <Samples>
                        <Sample CssClass="mb-5" SnippetComponent=typeof(ConfigurationDefaultsSnippet) Heading="FontAwesomeDefaults" />
                    </Samples>
                </SampleTab>
            </Tabs>
        </SampleTabs>
    </div>

    <h2>Precedence</h2>

    <ol>
        <li>An explicit parameter on the component.</li>
        <li>The nearest enclosing <code>FontAwesomeDefaults</code>.</li>
        <li>Options registered with <code>AddJeninFontAwesome</code>.</li>
        <li>The built-in library default.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Configurable values</h2>

    <table class="table table-striped align-middle">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Property</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Built-in default</th>
                <th>Affects</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>IconStyle</code></td>
                <td><code>IconStyle?</code></td>
                <td>Solid</td>
                <td>Style used when <code>Icon.IconStyle</code> is omitted.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Typeface</code></td>
                <td><code>Typeface?</code></td>
                <td>Classic</td>
                <td>Typeface used when <code>Icon.Typeface</code> is omitted.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>IconSize</code></td>
                <td><code>IconSize?</code></td>
                <td>X01</td>
                <td>Size used when <code>IconSize</code> is omitted.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Decorative</code></td>
                <td><code>bool?</code></td>
                <td>Inferred per component</td>
                <td>Global accessibility mode &mdash; see <a class="link-primary" href="accessibility">Accessibility</a>.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
        A <code>null</code> property means "no configured default": the built-in default is used instead, so an empty
        <code>AddJeninFontAwesome()</code> call changes nothing.
    </div>
</div>
